course: dictionary
lesson: 1264
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and a capital letter can tell you which one. Burton with a capital B is a name: a surname, or a place such as the town of Burton upon Trent. But in «go for a burton» the word belongs to a slang phrase, and the whole phrase means something different.
explain: Slang is informal language that people use with friends. In the story, the Rat finds beer labelled «Old Burton» and says, «Now we shall be able to mull some ale!» Here Burton is the name of a beer, and mulled ale is beer warmed with spices. The words around Burton tell you it is a drink.
explain: «My holiday plans have gone for a burton.» does not mean the plans went anywhere. The clue is gone, which tells you something has been lost or ruined. Try your meaning in the sentence: «My holiday plans have been ruined.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Burton is a noun. As a name, it always gets a capital letter.
fact: «Go for a burton» is a phrase from UK slang.
fact: «Go for a burton» means to be lost, broken, ruined or killed, and people often say it as a joke.
fact: The phrase comes from RAF slang in the Second World War, when it was used for a pilot who was killed.
fact: Burton upon Trent is an English town famous for brewing beer.
exercise: «The Rat finds the beer is Old Burton.» In this sentence, what is Burton? | A slang phrase meaning ruined | *A name, the name of a beer | A sort of warm drink with spices | A kind of pilot
exercise: «My plans have gone for a burton.» What does this slang phrase mean? | *Ruined or lost | Very large and loud | Made even better | A trip by boat
exercise: Why does Burton have a capital letter in «Burton upon Trent»? | Because it is slang | Because it is the first word of a sentence | *Because it is the name of a place | Because it is a long word
test: «My holiday plans have gone for a burton.» Are the plans fine or ruined? | *Ruined and lost | Made bigger and better | Fine and on track
test: Burton upon Trent is famous for what? | Growing grapes | *Brewing beer | Making shoes | Building ships
exam: What is «mulled ale»? | Juice from a fruit | Cold water | *Beer warmed with spices | Milk heated in a pan
